{"BlockedEmail.should_block? performs non-atomic read-increment-save of match_count, causing lost increments under concurrent signup requests": 0.8636263012886047, "validate_each calls BlockedEmail.should_block?(value) without guarding against nil or blank values, causing NoMethodError when value =~ regexp is called on nil email values during validation": 0.520232617855072, "rejectedEmails array is initialized once on the controller prototype and never cleared, causing valid emails to be incorrectly blocked if they match previously rejected values across signup attempts": 0.7001757025718689, "Signup failure response exposes raw validation errors via user.errors.to_hash and echoes user-provided values back, potentially leaking internal validation details and creating XSS risk if rendered unsafely": 0.548599123954773, "Frontend only checks result.errors.email but ActiveModel::Errors#to_hash may not include email key if validation failed on different attribute, breaking the client-side blocked email recording logic": 0.14447936415672302, "Comment stating last_match_at indicates whether emails have ever been blocked is now inaccurate since it's updated for any match attempt including action_type :do_nothing records": 0.1631283015012741}